    apply: "Write down three ways your life should be distinct because you belong to God, such as honesty, generosity or purity of speech. Choose one to focus on this week. Look for a way to show kindness to a neighbour who is not a believer.",
    activity: "Place ordinary objects and a special item, such as a Bible set aside for worship, on a table. Discuss what makes some things special: they are set apart for a particular use. Read 1 Peter 2:9-10 and list what believers are called and why.",
    takeHome: "Read Exodus 19:1-8, 1 Peter 2:1-12, Deuteronomy 7:6-11 and John 17:13-19. Write a paragraph on how to be in the world but not of it. Memorise 1 Peter 2:9.",
    prayer: "Thank God for choosing us and setting us apart. Ask for a life that shows his excellencies. Pray for neighbours who do not know him.",
    teacher: "Avoid language that sets believers against others in pride. Stress grace as the starting point. Be careful with learners in minority situations who may face real pressure because of their faith, and encourage them with Peter's words.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners what holy means at its root and why God sets his people apart.",
    mcq1: ["What do you shall be to me a kingdom of priests and a holy nation in Exodus 19:6 mean for Israel?", ["They were set apart to serve God among the nations", "They should avoid other nations", "They were above all law", "They were to become rulers by force"], 0, "They were to serve as God's representatives."],
    mcq2: ["According to 1 Peter 2:9, why is the church chosen?", ["To proclaim the excellencies of him who called us out of darkness", "To gain wealth", "To avoid suffering", "To judge others"], 0, "The purpose is to proclaim his excellencies."],
