    mcq1: ["What did Paul say about the Corinthians in 1 Corinthians 6:11?", ["You were washed, you were sanctified, you were justified", "You are without sin", "You are rich", "You are leaders"], 0, "They were washed, sanctified and justified."],
    mcq2: ["How does Hebrews 10:10 say we have been sanctified?", ["Through the offering of the body of Jesus Christ once for all", "Through repeated sacrifices", "Through our works", "Through the law"], 0, "By Christ's once-for-all offering."],
    tf: ["Believers must wait until they are mature before God considers them holy.", false, "In Christ they are already set apart as holy."],
    sa: ["What does it mean that believers are made holy in Christ?", ["christ", "sacrifice", "once for all", "standing", "saints", "set apart"], "A good answer says that by Christ's once-for-all sacrifice, believers are set apart as God's holy people at conversion, a secure standing from which they grow."],
